{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"files\":[{\"content\":\"#include <algorithm>\\n#include <iostream>\\n#include <utility>\\n#include <vector>\\n\\nusing namespace std;\\n\\nstatic const long long MOD = 1000000007LL;\\n\\nstatic long long modPow(long long base, long long exponent) {\\n    long long result = 1;\\n    while (exponent > 0) {\\n        if (exponent & 1LL) result = result * base % MOD;\\n        base = base * base % MOD;\\n        exponent >>= 1LL;\\n    }\\n    return result;\\n}\\n\\nint main() {\\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\\n\\n    int n, m;\\n    if (!(cin >> n >> m)) return 0;\\n\\n    vector<pair<int, int>> obstacles;\\n    obstacles.reserve(m);\\n    bool blockedStart = false;\\n    bool blockedEnd = false;\\n    for (int i = 0; i < m; ++i) {\\n        int row, col;\\n        cin >> row >> col;\\n        obstacles.emplace_back(row, col);\\n        if (row == 0 && col == 0) blockedStart = true;\\n        if (row == n - 1 && col == n - 1) blockedEnd = true;\\n    }\\n\\n    if (blockedStart || blockedEnd) {\\n        cout << 0 << '\\\\n';\\n        return 0;\\n    }\\n\\n    sort(obstacles.begin(), obstacles.end());\\n    obstacles.erase(unique(obstacles.begin(), obstacles.end()), obstacles.end());\\n\\n    const int maxSteps = 2 * (n - 1);\\n    vector<long long> factorial(maxSteps + 1), inverseFactorial(maxSteps + 1);\\n    factorial[0] = 1;\\n    for (int i = 1; i <= maxSteps; ++i)\\n        factorial[i] = factorial[i - 1] * i % MOD;\\n    inverseFactorial[maxSteps] = modPow(factorial[maxSteps], MOD - 2);\\n    for (int i = maxSteps; i > 0; --i)\\n        inverseFactorial[i - 1] = inverseFactorial[i] * i % MOD;\\n\\n    auto pathsBetween = [&](int row1, int col1, int row2, int col2) {\\n        int down = row2 - row1;\\n        int right = col2 - col1;\\n        int steps = down + right;\\n        return factorial[steps] * inverseFactorial[down] % MOD * inverseFactorial[right] % MOD;\\n    };\\n\\n    // Obstacles are ordered by row then column, so every valid predecessor\\n    // appears earlier. Each predecessor's contribution is independent.\\n    vector<long long> ways(obstacles.size());\\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < obstacles.size(); ++i) {\\n        const int row = obstacles[i].first;\\n        const int col = obstacles[i].second;\\n        long long total = pathsBetween(0, 0, row, col);\\n\\n        for (size_t begin = 0; begin < i; begin += 8) {\\n            const size_t end = min(i, begin + 8);\\n            long long partial = 0;\\n#pragma omp simd reduction(+:partial)\\n            for (size_t j = begin; j < end; ++j) {\\n                const int prevRow = obstacles[j].first;\\n                const int prevCol = obstacles[j].second;\\n                if (prevRow <= row && prevCol <= col) {\\n                    const long long contribution =\\n                        pathsBetween(prevRow, prevCol, row, col) * ways[j] % MOD;\\n                    partial += contribution;\\n                }\\n            }\\n            total = (total - partial % MOD + MOD) % MOD;\\n        }\\n        ways[i] = total;\\n    }\\n\\n    long long answer = pathsBetween(0, 0, n - 1, n - 1);\\n    for (size_t begin = 0; begin < obstacles.size(); begin += 8) {\\n        const size_t end = min(obstacles.size(), begin + 8);\\n        long long partial = 0;\\n#pragma omp simd reduction(+:partial)\\n        for (size_t j = begin; j < end; ++j) {\\n            const int row = obstacles[j].first;\\n            const int col = obstacles[j].second;\\n            if (row <= n - 1 && col <= n - 1) {\\n                const long long contribution =\\n                    pathsBetween(row, col, n - 1, n - 1) * ways[j] % MOD;\\n                partial += contribution;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        answer = (answer - partial % MOD + MOD) % MOD;\\n    }\\n\\n    cout << answer << '\\\\n';\\n    return 0;\\n}\\n\",\"path\":\"src/solution.cpp\"}],\"hypothesis\":\"Replacing the dense quadratic-grid DP with an obstacle-ordered path-count recurrence removes O(N^2) storage and reduces work to O(M^2) when obstacles are sparse. The predecessor contributions are independent within each obstacle, allowing legal SIMD reduction in small overflow-safe chunks while retaining the sequential dependency between obstacles.\",\"notes\":\"The recurrence sorts and deduplicates blocked coordinates, handles blocked endpoints directly, and uses exact modular binomial path counts. Worst-case time remains O(M^2), so dense obstacle sets may scale poorly; each SIMD chunk has at most eight terms, keeping its unreduced sum within signed 64-bit range. OpenMP SIMD pragmas do not require enabling threaded execution.\",\"research\":{\"queries\":[],\"urls\":[]},\"sources_kept\":[],\"transformations\":[\"Replace the N-by-N blocked-cell structure and rolling dense DP with a sorted, deduplicated obstacle list and modular combinatorial path recurrence.\",\"Apply SIMD reduction only to independent predecessor-contribution calculations, with the obstacle-to-obstacle outer dependency left sequential.\",\"Use chunks of at most eight modular contributions to bound unreduced signed 64-bit sums.\"]}"}}
